  "rationale": "The spec is throughput- and deadline-bound: 32 requests per 1us tick with all 32 results back within 0.44us of the tick. Only the 1-result-per-cycle families (pipelined, pipelined_m) can sustain 32 Msps and finish a 32-deep back-to-back batch inside the tick window; iterative and unrolled_k (1 result every several cycles) would queue the burst and blow the p99-batch bound, so they are excluded. The accuracy constraint max_abs_err<=2^-12 is met by modest W and N (W=14/N=12 is the likely minimal corner), so I bracket data_width 14..18 and n_iter 12..16 to map the area-vs-accuracy trade-off rather than oversizing. angle_guard 0..2 and frac_guard 0..2 keep the datapath lean for the min-luts_plus_ffs objective while still exposing the accuracy knobs. pipelined is the Fmax/latency-strong end; pipelined_m (m=2..4) is the area-reduction end; together they should span the feasible Pareto front. I split the budget evenly between the two because both are plausible front members and the hypervolume rewards covering the whole curve, not just the min-area corner the selection rule picks."
}

